  "title": "Kirby Problem 1.19",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $Y = Y_{1}\\#Y_{2}$ be a connected sum of 3-manifolds with $Y_{i} \\neq$\n$S^{3}$, for $i = 1, 2$. Let $\\Phi: Y \\to Y$ be a Dehn twist around the connected sum separating\n2-sphere, and assume $Y_{1}$ and $Y_{2}$ are such that $\\Phi$ is not isotopic to the identity. Does\nthere exist a knot $K \\subseteq Y$ such that $K$ and $\\Phi(K)$ are not ambiently isotopic?",
